## Fee Clarification: Exit Load
### Reusable Support Snippet

  • Exit load is a charge levied by the mutual fund when units are redeemed before the fund‑specified exit‑load period ends; it does not apply to redemptions made after that period.
  • The exit‑load period varies by scheme (e.g., 0–30 days, 30–90 days) and is defined in the scheme’s offer document; it is not a universal lock‑in for all funds.
  • The percentage of exit load differs across schemes (e.g., 0.5% for some equity funds, 1% for certain debt funds) and is disclosed

**Official Sources:**
  - https://www.sebi.gov.in/legal/circulars/jun-2009/exit-load-mutual-funds_3555.html
  - https://www.amfiindia.com/investor-corner/knowledge-center/exit-load

